  Thigh and lower-leg lengths are scaled by 125/104 (1.20192307692308):
    thigh:    0.17472 m -> 0.21 m
    lower leg: 0.208 m -> 0.25 m
  Leg cross-sectional dimensions and material density are unchanged. Therefore each
  leg-link mass scales linearly with length, its center of mass scales only along
  the length axis, and its inertia tensor uses anisotropic constant-density scaling.
  The physical closed chain has 0.428495192308 kg of scaled rear-link mass that is
  absent from this serial URDF. That mass is lumped into the corresponding upper and
  lower leg links for training. The base-link mass is adjusted so the complete robot
  mass remains 24 kg. Lumped-link COM locations are retained and their inertia tensors
  are scaled by the lumped mass ratio as an open-chain approximation.
-->
